    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In the midst of a boring and monotonous &quot;ordinary&quot; life, the protagonist, &quot;I,&quot; begins to frequently dream of childhood aspirations for some unknown reason. There are no significant memories, and the elementary school days are far away, to the extent that I haven't even received any notifications about reunions.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >One day, on an otherwise unremarkable morning, while commuting, &quot;I&quot; unexpectedly wanders into the childhood room once inhabited. It is a world where the boundary between dreams and reality is blurred. Memories of childhood, which had transformed into vague and pastoral images over many years, start to regain their original clarity.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Amidst a mix of nostalgia and anxiety, &quot;I&quot; is forced to confront my past. Will &quot;I&quot; be able to return to the real world from this labyrinth of memories? And what changes will this encounter with the past bring to &quot;my&quot; life?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3443030/extras/7d8c7a9e322c2178a5f111d714fec731.avif?t=1742179588\" data-has-big width=800 height=450 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >[Game Overview]</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >CLASS 3, THIRD GRADE is a 3D first-person perspective escape game. Players take on the role of the protagonist, &quot;I,&quot; exploring a nostalgic childhood room, collecting items necessary for escape, and solving various puzzles in order to return to the real world.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >[Game Features]</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A game world that faithfully recreates the atmosphere of the 1980s</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Experience a childhood where nostalgia and reality intersect</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Multiple endings: The truth changes depending on your choices</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game is not only &quot;my&quot; story but also &quot;your&quot; story</p></li></ul>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In the midst of a boring and monotonous &quot;ordinary&quot; life, the protagonist, &quot;I,&quot; begins to frequently dream of childhood aspirations for some unknown reason. There are no significant memories, and the elementary school days are far away, to the extent that I haven't even received any notifications about reunions.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >One day, on an otherwise unremarkable morning, while commuting, &quot;I&quot; unexpectedly wanders into the childhood room once inhabited. It is a world where the boundary between dreams and reality is blurred. Memories of childhood, which had transformed into vague and pastoral images over many years, start to regain their original clarity.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Amidst a mix of nostalgia and anxiety, &quot;I&quot; is forced to confront my past. Will &quot;I&quot; be able to return to the real world from this labyrinth of memories? And what changes will this encounter with the past bring to &quot;my&quot; life?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3443030/extras/7d8c7a9e322c2178a5f111d714fec731.avif?t=1742179588\" data-has-big width=800 height=450 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >[Game Overview]</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >CLASS 3, THIRD GRADE is a 3D first-person perspective escape game. Players take on the role of the protagonist, &quot;I,&quot; exploring a nostalgic childhood room, collecting items necessary for escape, and solving various puzzles in order to return to the real world.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >[Game Features]</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A game world that faithfully recreates the atmosphere of the 1980s</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Experience a childhood where nostalgia and reality intersect</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Multiple endings: The